1. Grant of Rights

Subject to the conditions below, permission is hereby granted, free of
charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated
documentation files (the "Software"), to use, copy, modify, merge,
publish, distribute, and sublicense copies of the Software, and to
permit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, provided
that the Software and any derivative works are not used for any
commercial purpose (see Section 3).

2. Attribution

Any copy or derivative work of the Software, in whole or in substantial
part, must:

  a. retain this license notice in full;
  b. clearly credit the original author, Likolisu, and include a link
     to the source repository (https://github.com/awdrrawd/BC-AEE);
  c. clearly credit contributors InkerBot
     (https://github.com/InkerBot) and Tao MUSE.

This attribution must be presented in a place a user would reasonably
find it, such as a README, an "About" page, a copyright notice section,
or a prominent location on the release page.

3. Non-Commercial Use Only

The Software, and any derivative work based on it, may not be used for
any purpose intended for or directed toward direct or indirect
commercial advantage, including but not limited to:

  a. selling copies of the Software or any derivative work;
  b. offering the Software or any derivative work as part of a paid
     subscription, paid membership content, or any other paid service;
  c. monetizing distribution or use of the Software through
     advertisements, sponsorships, or other paid promotional
     placements;
  d. any other activity that directly or indirectly generates
     commercial revenue based on the Software or its derivatives.

If you are unsure whether a particular use qualifies as commercial,
please contact the original author before proceeding.

4. Derivative Works

Subject to Sections 2 and 3, you may freely modify the Software and
distribute it as a derivative work. Any such derivative work remains
subject to the terms of this license — anyone who receives it must be
granted the same rights and be subject to the same obligations as
under this license.

5. Disclaimer of Warranty

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF
MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT.
IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY
CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT,
TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE
SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
